No test in t/ reads the cpanfile, so a prerequisite that the code uses but that is missing in the cpanfile stays unnoticed. The missing https prerequisite of the cpanfile is exactly such a case.

Decide: a new t/cpanfile.t reads the cpanfile and checks every prerequisite that the code uses. /home/getty/dev/p5-www-vastai/t/cpanfile.t is the pattern to follow.

2026-10-20 09:17 Worker k6-k10: done. t/cpanfile.t reads the cpanfile, builds %requires and checks HTTP::Cookies, LWP, LWP::Protocol::https, Moo, MooX::Types::MooseLike::Base and Safe::Isa; HTTP::Request and HTTP::Response stay out, they come with LWP. The test checks a file, not behaviour, so it is not red against the old lib; the failure mode was shown by restoring the old cpanfile: the test fails on LWP::Protocol::https. The file follows the pattern of p5-www-vastai/t/cpanfile.t (File::Spec, FindBin, core modules only) instead of Path::Tiny, to keep the cpanfile free of a new test dependency.

2026-10-20 09:21 Done: new t/cpanfile.t reads the cpanfile and checks HTTP::Cookies, LWP, LWP::Protocol::https, Moo, MooX::Types::MooseLike::Base and Safe::Isa. HTTP::Request and HTTP::Response are not declared, they come via LWP -> HTTP::Message. The test was red against the old cpanfile ('LWP::Protocol::https is a declared prerequisite' failed), it is green now. Commit 0ab41e5.

